\par\par \b \uc2 Canada Afternoon: C$ Ends Higher, But Retreats From High\b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 21:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended higher Wednesday as it followed through on strength from Tuesday and benefited from broader weakness in the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 But the Canadian unit was unable to maintain the six-week high it hit in earlier trading and retreated from it in quieter afternoon trading.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.0312 at 3:35 p.m. EST (2035 GMT), from C$1.0340 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), and from C$1.0362 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In late morning trading it touched a low at C$1.0276, its lowest level since Jan 19, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian unit rallied on Tuesday after the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  left its overnight target rate at 0.25% but issued a policy statement with a more aggressive tilt on monetary tightening than many had anticipated.\par \par \uc2 At least some of the strengthening Wednesday was attributable to an extension of that rally.\par \par \uc2 "I would say it's probably more follow through from yesterday in terms of the more hawkish tone that came out of the statement," said Kevin Chau, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at IDEAGlobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar's gains Tuesday also came in association with a broader retreat by the U.S. dollar and shift back into the euro and other risk-oriented \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after some Greek austerity measures were well received by markets.\par \par \uc2 "It's basically just a risk acceptance story. All the majors are appreciating against the dollar," said Tyson Wright, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Custom House, a global payments firm in Victoria, British Columbia.\par \par \uc2 IDEAGlobal's Chau said the market is waiting for monetary policy meetings at the Bank of England and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and critical February nonfarm payrolls data in the U.S. on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the U.S. dollar will likely trade in a range between C$1.0250 and C$1.0350, he said. "I don't see it going below C$1.0200," Chau.\par \par \uc2 Longer-term, the U.S. dollar will head back higher against its Canadian counterpart, he said.\par \par \uc2 Custom House's Wright also said the U.S. unit could head towards the C$1.0200 area, but believes a break below that is unlikely.\par \par \uc2 Wright said strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could ultimately prompt verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In its Tuesday policy statement, the bank said the persistent strength of the Canadian dollar and the low absolute level of U.S. demand continue to act as significant drags on economic activity in Canada.\par \par \uc2 In domestic data Wednesday, Canada's official international reserves rose $365 million in February, the federal Finance Department reported.\par \par \uc2 At Feb. 26, the reserves of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and other monetary assets totaled $57.342 billion, up from $56.977 billion a month earlier.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, building permits data for January and the Ivey Purchasing Managers Index for February will be released, and the federal budget for the 2010-11 fiscal year will be unveiled.\par \par \uc2 These are the exchange rates at 3:25 p.m. EST (2035 GMT), 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), and late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/CAD     1.0312      1.0340     1.0362 \par    EUR/CAD     1.4135      1.4090     1.4105 \par    CAD/JPY      85.80       85.88      85.66 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Don Curren, Dow Jones Newswires; 416-306-2020; don.curren@dowjones.com [ 03-03-10 1537ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1158   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100303e633000dg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
