\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Extends Gains; US Data Encouraging\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 905 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2010\par 15:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)-- The dollar marched higher against the euro and U.K. pound Tuesday as a U.S. economy increasingly outpacing its peers contrasted with weaker-than-expected euro zone economic data and lingering concern over Greek debt.\par \par \uc2 Data released Tuesday showed the freefall in U.S. home prices had been eased, with aid from government efforts.\par \par \uc2 "You could argue there's a vein of thinking that the U.S. is pulling out [of recession] slightly ahead of Europe," said John McCarthy, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at ING Capital Markets in New York.\par \par \uc2 The small improvement in home price data only cements the idea of the U.S. leading the way out of the economic doldrums, McCarthy said.\par \par \uc2 The U.K. recovery, meanwhile, could lag as the euro zone sputters, a Bank of England official said Tuesday, putting pressure on the pound.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday morning in New York, the euro was at $1.3558 from $1.3597 late Monday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y90.78 from Y91.13, while the euro was at Y123.08 from Y123.94. The U.K. pound was at $1.5435 from $1.5480. The dollar was at CHF1.0814 from CHF1.0761.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 80.705 from 80.552.\par \par \uc2 The S&P Case-Shiller home-price indexes showed continuing improvement in December, according to the report released Tuesday. The 10-city and 20-city composites saw annual declines of 2.4% and 3.1%, respectively. Economists had expected the 20-City index to fall 3.2%.\par \par \uc2 The two indexes have seen improvements in their annual rates of change every month since the beginning of 2009. On a seasonally adjusted basis, both the 10-city and 20-city indexes rose 0.3% in December over November.\par \par \uc2 "Even in the areas that are still soft, the declines in price are much reduced," said Alan Ruskin, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy for RBS Securities in Stamford, Ct.\par \par \uc2 The slow-but-steady improvement in many measures of the U.S. economic recovery contrasted a slip in Germany's Ifo business expectations survey index, which unexpectedly fell, casting a pall on the pace of a euro-zone recovery. The February index fell to 95.2 from 95.8 in January, its first drop in 11 months; analysts had expected the Ifo business-sentiment index to have risen to 96.4.\par \par \uc2 The U.K. pound also slipped as Bank of England Governor Mervyn King said weaker euro zone growth could dent a nascent U.K. recovery. Giving evidence to U.K. lawmakers Tuesday, King said recovery in the euro zone "appears to have stalled."\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the BOE would restart its bond-buying program, called quantitative easing, King said: "I don't know, but we stand ready to do whatever seems appropriate."\par \par \uc2 A restart of the bond-buying program would likely weigh on the pound.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the euro spiked against the Swiss franc during Asian trading to CHF1.4684 from CHF1.4630. Five dealers in Tokyo said speculators bought amid talk in the market the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  had been buying. The SNB, as is its policy, wouldn't comment.\par \par \uc2 The SNB is thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on three occasions this month, including an unusual move late afternoon Feb. 12 just as the U.S. markets were heading into a long holiday weekend.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly since March 2009 in an attempt to stave off the threat of deflation, or a persistent decline in consumer prices, and to bolster the Swiss exports; the euro's broad weakness since the beginning of the year, due in part to concerns over the fiscal health of the weaker members in the euro zone, has forced the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Morning \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Canadian dollar was lower Tuesday morning as it remained under the sway of broader fluctuations in risk appetite without any significant economic data or other domestic factors to provide guidance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.0439 from C$1.0423 late Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 News that Canadian property company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brookfield Asset Management Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is readying a bid to take a large stake in U.S. mall owner \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Growth Properties Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . could put some pressure on the Canadian dollar in coming sessions, although details of the proposed deal haven't yet been released.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BMO Capital Markets said the move higher by the U.S./Canadian dollar pair in earlier trading was mainly players with short positions in the U.S. dollar bailing out as that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rallied last night.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "So far we have seen some small sellers around 1.0450 but our gut tells us that overall risk aversion will push this pair higher," BMO said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We expect to see decent offers at 1.0480 and then 1.0530, but it appears the pair will remain range bound today," BMO said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654; bradley.davis@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Don Curren in Toronto, Fabio Alves and Kathleen Madigan in New York, Natasha Brereton and Paul Hannon in London and Takashi Mochizuki in Tokyo contributed to this article.) [ 02-23-10 0954ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100223e62n000a3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
