\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-POLL-Most Canada dealers see bank keeping rate pledge\b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2009\par 18:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * No rate change expected in Dec and Jan\par \par \uc2 * Slim chance of BoC \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets\par \par \uc2 * Dealers say quantitative easing also unlikely (Adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Frank Pingue\par \par \uc2 TORONTO, Dec 4 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  is likely to stick to its conditional pledge to keep its key interest rate at near-zero levels through the second quarter of 2010, most of Canada's primary securities dealers predicted on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Most also saw only a marginal chance the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would opt to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets or introduce some form of \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quantitative easing -- effectively printing money to buy market\par securities -- at some time over the next 12 months.\par  "The inflation outlook is fairly subdued, especially with\par the (Canadian) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  possibly headed towards parity," said\par Sal Guatieri, senior economist at BMO Capital Markets.\par  "Everything is on track ... I don't think the Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canada will adjust its economic outlook. Inflation is likely to get back to target in third quarter 2011."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All 12 of Canada's dealers, surveyed by Reuters after better-than-expected jobs data for November, forecast the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would stay committed to its pledge of low interest rates at its Dec. 8 policy announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in April it would keep the overnight rate at a record low 0.25 percent, as long as inflation remains in check, until at least the end of June 2010. It has reiterated its intention to do this many times.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The poll was conducted after the release of data that showed Canada's economy added 79,000 jobs in November, surpassing analysts' expectations for a gain of 15,000. [ID:nN04141170]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That data followed a report earlier this week that showed Canada's economy crawled out of recession in the third quarter after three quarters of contraction. [ID:nN30349047]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A report out last month showed inflation returned to Canada in October after a short deflationary bout but prices remained tame and are not expected to sway the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2 . [ID:nN1892543]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What rate action do you expect at the next three \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  decisions?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  PRIMARY DEALER                   DEC      JAN    MARCH\par                                ACTION   ACTION   ACTION\par  BMO CAPITAL MARKETS          NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  CASGRAIN & CO                NO MOVE  NO MOVE  UP 25\par  CIBC WORLD MARKETS           NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  DESJARDINS SECURITIES        NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  DEUTSCHE BANK SECURITIES     NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  HSBC SECURITIES              NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  LAURENTIAN BANK SECURITIES   NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  BOFA MERRILL LYNCH           NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  NATIONAL BANK                NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  RBC CAPITAL MARKETS          NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  SCOTIA CAPITAL               NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 TORONTO-DOMINION BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2         NO MOVE  NO MOVE  NO MOVE\par  Which quarter do you expect the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2 