\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Only Fleeting C$ Boost From Russian Interest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Don Curren   \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2009\par 18:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TORONTO (Dow Jones)--News that Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is edging closer to adding Canadian dollars to its reserves will likely have only a fleeting impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with overall U.S. dollar gyrations playing a bigger role in its short-term movements.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied sharply in overnight trading Wednesday, extending earlier gains after the Russian news agency Interfax reported that the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's head of open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sergei Shvetsov, said in comments to the State Duma the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is undergoing "technical preparations for \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Canadian dollars."\par \par \uc2 In late morning trading, the U.S. dollar had recovered to the C$1.0500 area from an intraday low at C$1.0452, but remained down significantly from C$1.0592 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 Analysts cautioned against attributing too much significance to the news, linking instead the Canadian dollar's gains to the pervasive weakness in the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "On a day when the dollar has fallen to new lows [for 2009] against the euro, fallen below par against the Swiss franc, is down over a cent against the British pound, [and at] new lows against the yen since January, I don't know if we really need the Russians to be buying the Canadian dollar to signal a Canadian dollar rally," said Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "If we were to talk about the Canadian dollar in a vacuum, I would say it's as good as any story out there, but I would say it probably gives a news item too much credibility," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The Canadian dollar was already stronger ahead of those comments on the back of the U.S. dollar being sold generally," said Adam Cole, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "It's partly CAD-specific and it's partly just the dollar looking very sad [against] all the majors," he said.\par \par \uc2 Another reason not to exaggerate the significance of the Russian news is that the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intention was already known. In September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first deputy chairman Alexei Ulyukayev said that Canadian and Australian dollars could be added to reserves in the future.\par \par \uc2 Russia have also acknowledged liquidity issues associated with expanding into \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Canadian dollar.\par \par \uc2 "In the past, when the Russians have talked about the Canadian dollar, they've acknowledged...the lack of sufficient supply," Chandler said.\par \par \uc2 More broadly, the Canadian dollar has limited prospects as a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  globally, in part because of liquidity constraints with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the country's bond market.\par \par \uc2 "There doesn't seem to be a whole lot of room for the Canadian dollar as a reserve asset," Chandler said.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the Canadian dollar will continue to be driven by overall U.S. dollar movements, and in recent trading the greenback has been moving lower against the euro and other key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar is under pressure and risk-oriented assets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are prospering because of the abundance of liquidity in global financial markets, Chandler said.\par \par \uc2 RBC's Cole said the Canadian dollar appears poised to strengthen further, but its potential appreciation could be curbed by fears among traders that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  could once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally against it.\par \par \uc2 "I think there is a general sense that the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  is not comfortable and will try and talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down. That will slow the pace of appreciation, but ultimately won't stop it," he said.\par \par \uc2 RBC expects the Canadian dollar will again test parity against its U.S. counterpart, but not likely until the New Year.\par \par \uc2 -Don Curren, Dow Jones Newswires; 416-306-2020; don.curren@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Don Curren, a reporter based in Toronto, has covered Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income markets for more than 10 years. He can be reached at 416-306-2020 or at don.curren@dowjones.com.)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments [ 11-25-09 1249ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091125e5bp000cx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
