\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Remains Under Pressure On Asian Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 1,102 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2009\par 15:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar remained near 15-month lows against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in morning trading Wednesday, as positive Asian economic data continued to boost optimism into the North American session for a global economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The euro overnight gained strongly on the positive data, hitting $1.5049, close to its 2009 high of $1.5064. If the euro breaks through its 2009 high in New York trading, it could rally beyond $1.52, according to \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  analysts.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks are expected to open higher. With no important U.S. economic data on tap and with the U.S. and Canadian Veterans Day holidays keeping trading subdued, higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to extend their gains if stocks rally.\par \par \uc2 In early morning trading, the euro was at $1.5016 from $1.4978 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y89.88 from Y89.84, while the euro was at Y134.98 from Y134.58. The U.K pound was at $1.6643 from $1.6728. The dollar was at CHF1.0057 from CHF1.0083.\par \par \uc2 The Dollar Index, a trade-weighted basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 74.943 from 75.052.\par \par \uc2 "The momentum and the conviction that the Fed will not raise rates any time soon, coupled with the fact that the major central banks continue to provide liquidity liberally, the fundamental force weighing on the dollar persists," said Marc Chandler, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to its lowest level against the euro in more than two weeks in overnight trading; the euro remained well above $1.50 after failing Tuesday to muster the strength to rally past the psychologically important level as U.S. stocks wavered.\par \par \uc2 But the positive Asian economic data bolstered risk appetite, leading to gains in commodities, most Asian stocks and in European bourses so far Wednesday, though the slow trading day--with U.S. bond markets closed--could also stall the euro's gains.\par \par \uc2 "The China news is stirring the stock market higher, but without any kind of further news [in the North American session], I have a feeling we're more likely to see a stall," in the euro's gains against the dollar, said Brian Dolan, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .com in Bedminster, N.J.\par \par \uc2 The data showed China's industrial output for October surged 16.1% from a year earlier, outpacing a 15.5% rise forecast in a Dow Jones Newswires survey of economists.\par \par \uc2 In Japan, machinery orders rose by 10.5% in September, which \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  economists said was a good sign for "the sustainability of growth," and which was much stronger than the 3.2% increase predicted by a Dow Jones survey of economists.\par \par \uc2 Also overnight, sterling lurched sharply lower after Bank of England Governor Mervyn King said in a press conference accompanying the BOE's quarterly inflation report that recent sterling weakness would be supportive to an export-led recovery.\par \par \uc2 The weakness reflected expectations that U.K. interest rates will remain super-low for a long period, as well as investors' anxiety about the U.K.'s expanding debt burden, which could hamper the country's economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 This is not the first time that King has referred to sterling weakness in these terms. Nonetheless, the pound sank from a spike to $1.6798 against the dollar to the $1.6650 area. It has since recovered slightly, but remains weaker on the day.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, China came under new pressure from Pacific Rim countries Wednesday to let it \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise, even as the U.S. stepped up its commitment to a strong dollar ahead of a regional summit.\par \par \uc2 As finance ministers from the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum were preparing to call for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility--generally code for a rise in the yuan--U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner, gave a particularly spirited defense of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I believe deeply that it's very important for the U.S. and the economic health of the U.S. that we maintain a strong dollar," Geithner said in Tokyo before joining fellow APEC finance ministers in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "We bear special responsibility for trying to make sure that we are implementing policy in the U.S. that will sustain confidence not just among American investors and ... savers but investors around the world" that the U.S. will fix its budgetary problems as its economy improves.\par \par \uc2 In Beijing, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a rare change to the official language of its exchange-rate policy, giving a nod to concerns about the declining dollar and surging capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  said in a quarterly report it will take into account "changes in international capital flows and the trends of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in exchange-rate policy.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   Canada Morning \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Canadian dollar was up sharply Wednesday morning and was outperforming a broad range of other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in response to strength in equities and crude oil futures and a general interest in riskier assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar was at C$1.0453 from C$1.0500 late Tuesday. It dropped to a session low at C$1.0434, its lowest level since Oct. 22, according to EBS via CQG, before rebounding modestly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the Canadian dollar is the top performer in the overnight session, and it looks for more Canadian dollar strength against the U.S. dollar, and more Canadian dollar outperformance generally, as the risk environment remains positive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think you're seeing a little bit of momentum, technical type (U.S. dollar) selling, as well, over the last 24 hours or so," said David Bradley, director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Scotia Capital.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market players appear to be targeting a move toward the C$1.0325-50 area, he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A move toward that area could prompt more verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and government officials, but actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains extremely unlikely, Bradley said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are no significant Canadian data releases Wednesday, and bond trading is closed for the Remembrance Day holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trading in the Canadian dollar has been notably light so far Wednesday, Bradley said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Don Curren in Toronto, Katie Martin in London and William Mallard in Singapore contributed to this article.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654; bradley.davis@dowjones.com [ 11-11-09 0915ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091111e5bb0008x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
