\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-\uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  says China  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy "great risk"\b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2009\par 23:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * BoC \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be linked to inflation target\par \par \uc2  * Studying of price targeting merits further study\par \par \uc2  By David Ljunggren and Randall Palmer\par \par \uc2  OTTAWA, Oct 28 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy poses a great risk and it is a top priority of global policy makers to work toward a change, \uc2 Bank of Canada Governor Mark Carney\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  "They are running a great risk with this policy. It is a cause of some of the imbalances in the global economy. It is a contributing factor to some of the vulnerabilities that have existed and were realized," Carney told a Senate committee.\par \par \uc2  "It is a top priority I think for all policy makers to work with the Chinese and develop a suite of policies across all major economies, including China, that are consistent with moving off of this policy."\par \par \uc2  The Chinese yuan has been virtually repegged against the dollar since mid-2008, contributing to the further buildup of the country's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2  Making his second appearance before a parliamentary committee this week, Carney repeated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's view that the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should be seen in the context of achieving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2 percent inflation target.\par \par \uc2  "We should only use our tools that we have, which include \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a manner that is consistent with achieving the inflation target. And that would be the objective of any policy action that we would take," he said.\par \par \uc2  Carney also repeated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not target a specific rate for the Canadian dollar and has options, including credit and quantitative easing, if it feels further easing is needed after cutting interest rates to a record low.\par \par \uc2  He said the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  believes it is worth studying further the possibility of switching from its current inflation target to one of targeting price levels.\par \par \uc2  The distinction is a fine one, but under price-level targeting the bank would aim for a specific numeric value in the consumer price index and would try to reverse any past deviation from that target.\par \par \uc2  If the target were overshot, this would mean temporarily tighter monetary policy than otherwise would have been warranted.\par \par \uc2  Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current policy, which expires at the end of 2011, it tries to keep inflation at 2 percent and ignores any past deviations.\par \par \uc2  "It's too early to come to any conclusions. I would say the price-level targeting research merits continued focus," Carney told the Senate committee.\par \par \uc2  He would not say whether the bank thought it was useful, if inflation targeting were retained, to lower the target from 2 percent.  (Writing by Jeffrey Hodgson; Editing by Leslie Adler)   \par \par \uc2 CANADA-ECONOMY/BANKOFCANADA (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|CANT|ABN|E|U|RBN|M|D|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091028e5as001xg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
