\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  no good unless policy backs it-BoC\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2009\par 16:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Needs complementary policy moves to work\par \par \uc2 * Says current policies are appropriate (Adds quotes)\par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, Oct 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually does not work without complementary policy moves, \uc2 Bank of Canada Governor Mark Carney\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained an option, but Carney said it rarely worked long-term: "History has shown that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in and of itself, without backing policy moves, or policy moves that are consistent with the direction of that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , seldom is effective over the longer term."\par \par \uc2 He pointed out that the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  only targets inflation, not the Canadian dollar, though it does watch the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely.\par \par \uc2 "What is important ultimately is that we have sufficient instruments to achieve our inflation target ... The objective of the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  is to conduct, across a suite of policy options that we have, all those policies in order to achieve the 2 percent CPI inflation target," he said.\par \par \uc2 "In that context, the exchange rate is an important factor."\par \par \uc2 Carney repeated that the strength in the Canadian dollar had more than fully offset favorable developments in the economy since July and was a risk to recovery.\par \par \uc2 "The recent movements have caused a shifting out in the profile of when we will return to our inflation target by one quarter, and within that context the bank retains considerable options to provide additional stimulus, were it required, in order to achieve that," he said.\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policies, including its conditional commitment to keep interest rates unchanged through the middle of next year, were appropriate to meeting its 2 percent inflation target over the medium term.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar -- which has retreated on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent remarks -- dropped to its lowest level in almost three weeks this week as commodity prices fell and risk-averse investors moved back into the perceived safety of the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 By late morning the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CAD=> was at C$1.0652 to the U.S. dollar, or 93.88 U.S. cents, its lowest level since Oct. 6. (Reporting by Randall Palmer and David Ljunggren)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CANADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|CANT|ABN|E|U|RBN|M|D|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091027e5ar001om\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw98\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1470\pichgoal600
