\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Canadian dollar seen in tight range over next year\b0\par\par\uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2009\par 19:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * C$ seen rising to C$1.090 per US$ in a month\par \par \uc2 * Little chance seen of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Commodities expected to help C$ stay above 90 U.S. cents\par \par \uc2 By Frank Pingue\par \par \uc2 TORONTO, Sept 2 (Reuters) - Canada's dollar, whose strong rally has caused concern for the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is now expected to stick in a tight range near current levels over the next year, a monthly Reuters poll showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 But forecasts varied widely, reflecting a still-uncertain economic outlook, with six forecasts calling for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reach parity with the U.S. dollar in the next 12 months and another six calling for it to fall back to around 83 U.S. cents over the next year.\par \par \uc2 The poll also showed experts felt there was just a 17.5 percent chance that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to rein in the Canadian dollar's surge off the four-year low it stumbled to in March.\par \par \uc2 At 12:15 p.m. (1615 GMT) on Wednesday, the Canadian dollar was at C$1.1068 to the U.S. dollar, or 90.35 U.S. cents, which put it about 18 percent above the March low.\par \par \uc2 In one month, the Canadian dollar is expected to be worth C$1.090 to the U.S. dollar, or 91.74 U.S. cents, according to the median estimate of 52 strategists polled by Reuters between Aug. 27 and Sept. 1.\par \par \uc2 In three, six and 12 months, the median estimate of those polled had the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady at C$1.100 to the U.S. dollar, or 90.91 U.S. cents.\par \par \uc2 The most bearish forecast came from ING Financial Markets, which expects the Canadian dollar to fall to C$1.30 to the U.S. dollar, or 76.92 U.S. cents, in 12 months. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not traded that low since March.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of the good news is already in the Canadian dollar, which looks to have run ahead of the commodity story and does not take enough account of the fall in the Canadian trade surplus," said Chris Turner, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at ING.\par \par \uc2 But others feel the commodity backdrop, which is often a key influence on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the nature of Canada's exports, could be one of the main driving forces of the Canadian dollar in coming months.\par \par \uc2 Signs of global economic health have helped generate a meaty recovery in oil prices, but they still remain well off last year's record above $147.\par \par \uc2 "Despite official concerns about Canadian dollar strength the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue to appreciate in the months ahead, supported by a generally softer U.S. dollar and further strength in commodity prices," said Mitul Kotecha, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Calyon.\par \par \uc2 As the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has charged ahead this year, the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  issued warnings about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength threatening the domestic economy's recovery. Canada's finance minister also raised the possibility of policy makers \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. [ID:nN04143584]\par \par \uc2 But poll respondents pegged the chance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  going down that road as very low, saying they would take a more hands off approach and keep with its pledge to leave its key rate at a record low 0.25 percent until mid-2010.\par \par \uc2 "They risk their own credibility, especially as the drop in USD/CAD is not sufficient to justify the need for physical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " said Camilla Sutton and Sacha Tihanyi, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists at Scotia Capital.\par \par \uc2 "The BoC has a host of tools that they can use to help slow the pace of the drop in USD/CAD and we suspect these will be used long before physical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CANADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -DOLLAR-POLL|LANGEN|ABN|E|U|RBN|CANT|D|M    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090905e592000c9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
