\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Canadian dollar seen edging lower in coming months\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2009\par 17:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * C$ to ease to C$1.08 per US$ in a month\par \par \uc2 * Parity with greenback unlikely\par \par \uc2 * Focus firmly on \uc2 Bank of Canada\par \par \uc2 By Frank Pingue\par \par \uc2 TORONTO, Aug 5 (Reuters) - Canada's dollar will steadily back off the 10-month high reached earlier this week given talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and possible U.S. interest rate hikes, a monthly Reuters poll showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 And while results of the poll suggest the Canadian unit will not rise above its U.S. counterpart, a backdrop of lofty commodity prices should keep it from falling too far from current levels above 90 U.S. cents.\par \par \uc2 The forecasts varied widely, reflecting a still-uncertain economic outlook, with one forecaster calling for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise to par with the U.S. dollar within the next 12 months and another calling for it to fall as low as 76.92 cents.\par \par \uc2 At 11:35 a.m. (1535 GMT) on Wednesday, the Canadian dollar was at C$1.0730 to the U.S. dollar, or 93.20 U.S. cents, down from a 10-month high of C$1.0632 to the U.S. dollar, or 94.06 U.S. cents, it touched on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to be at C$1.080 to the U.S. dollar, or 92.59 U.S. cents, in one month, according to the median estimate of 46 strategists polled between Aug. 3 and 5. In three months, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fall further to C$1.105 to the U.S. dollar, or 90.50 U.S. cents.\par \par \uc2 In six months, it is expected to be worth C$1.107 to the U.S. dollar, or 90.33 U.S. cents, and in a year it could recover some of its slide and move to C$1.095 to the U.S. dollar, or 91.32 U.S. cents.\par \par \uc2 The bulk of the forecasts are rosier than in the last poll, when participants expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's performance would be hampered by sliding commodity prices. [ID:nN0265716]\par \par \uc2 But commodity prices have proved to be a key support to the Canadian dollar's 8 percent rally in July, and it only retreated this week after Canada's finance minister said steps could be taken to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ascent. [ID:nN04143584]\par \par \uc2 Those comments came about two weeks after the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  said the country's recession was virtually over, and said it was ready help stimulate the economy further, especially if a stronger dollar threatened to choke growth. [ID:nN23196742]\par \par \uc2 "Though the threat of (verbal) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to be reckoned with, the surge in commodity prices and hawkish comments by the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  ... should help to underpin the CAD in the near term," said Kenneth Broux, an economist at Lloyds TSB Corp Markets.\par \par \uc2 "The longer term calls for the upward trend in $/CAD to resume as U.S. interest rate expectations shift and the U.S. economy recovers."\par \par \uc2 According to a Reuters poll of primary dealers taken in July, the likelihood of a sluggish recovery means the U.S. Federal Reserve is not expected to hike interest rates until 2010 or later. [ID:nNAT004969]\par \par \uc2 If interest rates start rising, a likely sign that the global economy is improving, the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could also get a lift as it would likely mean more demand for some of the export commodities that Canada produces, notably oil.\par \par \uc2 "Though parity will begin to act as a magnet, we think parity on a sustainable basis is unlikely in 2009," said Camilla Sutton, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Scotia Capital.\par \par \uc2 "However, we believe that the overall trend will be one for a stronger CAD. The view is based on a positive outlook for commodities as the recovery in global growth takes root combined with a broadly weaker USD."\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CANADA-DOLLAR-POLL|LANGEN|ABN|E|U|RBN|CANT|D|M    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090808e585000a7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
