\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Canada's Flaherty talks of "steps" to slow C$ rise\b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2009\par 19:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Ottawa says measures could be taken to dampen C$\par \par \uc2 * Canadian dollar falls after remarks (Updates with \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  details; \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's close)\par \par \uc2 By Ka Yan Ng\par \par \uc2 PICKERING, Ontario, Aug 4 (Reuters) - Canada's finance minister raised the possibility on Tuesday of policy makers \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the Canadian dollar's sharp rise puts the fragile economic recovery at risk.\par \par \uc2 Immediately after Flaherty's comments, the Canadian dollar fell against the U.S. dollar after hitting a 10-month high earlier in the day.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters in Canada are strictly the domain of the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 , not the government, and so far few market players are betting the bank will step in to brake the appreciation.\par \par \uc2 "I won't substitute my views for those of the governor of the Bank (of Canada) ... We are concerned with any rapid changes in the valuation of the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  vis a vis the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... We watch that," Flaherty told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "There are some steps that could be taken to dampen that. There are, from time to time, indications of some speculation in the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is not justified in market terms," he said.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar rose as high as C$1.0632 to the U.S. dollar, or 94.06 U.S. cents, on Tuesday, up 1.3 percent from Friday, before paring gains. Monday was a market holiday in Canada.\par \par \uc2 After Flaherty spoke, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to C$1.0756, or 92.97 U.S. cents. It later rebounded to close at C$1.0745 to the U.S. dollar, or 93.07 U.S. cents, up from Friday's close of C$1.0775 to the U.S. dollar, or 92.81 U.S. cents.\par \par \uc2 Matthew Strauss, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 , said the reversal in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movement was caused entirely by Flaherty's comments rather than the more frequent reason of a change in U.S. risk sentiment.\par \par \uc2 "What the market really latched on to was his comments on there are some steps that could be taken to dampen the Canadian dollar rise," he said.\par \par \uc2 "It's the concern of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Strauss said.\par \par \uc2 Last month, \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Mark Carney\uc2  did not rule out taking additional policy action if the Canadian dollar remained persistently higher than the 87 U.S. cents projected in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly report.\par \par \uc2 Canadian exporters, the backbone of the economy, are hard hit by a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they receive most of their sales revenue in U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since September 1998 and Carney said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only effective if backed up by other policies. The bank retains "considerable flexibility" in this regard and will use that flexibility if necessary, he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its benchmark interest rate to a floor of 0.25 percent and if it wants to stimulate the economy further, it would have to resort to creating money and buying bonds in the market -- a step called quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 Potentially, Carney could do a combination of quantitative easing and selling of Canadian dollars to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Ka Yan Ng, writing by Louise Egan, additional reporting by Jennifer Kwan; editing by Rob Wilson)\par \par \uc2 CANADA-ECONOMY/DOLLAR  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|CANT|G|RNP|DNP|PGE    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090804e584001pk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
