\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  says lofty C$ a brake on growth\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2009\par 17:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, July 23 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not changed its policy for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but acknowledged that a lofty Canadian dollar is a risk to economic growth, \uc2 Governor Mark Carney\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The (Canadian) dollar is an important brake on the pace of growth right now," Carney said at a news conference after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released its Monetary Policy Report. "Further strength, volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is an important risk to the outlook."\par \par \uc2 In the report, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Canada's economy will pull out of its worst recession since the early 1990s this quarter. [ID:nN23196742] (Reporting by Louise Egan, writing by Frank Pingue; editing by Rob Wilson)\par \par \uc2 CANADA-ECONOMY/BANKOFCANADA/DOLLAR (URGENT)|LANGEN|CANT|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|ABN|RBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090726e57n000ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
