\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  an option, rarely effective-BoC\b0\par\par\uc2 126 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2009\par 21:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 REGINA, Saskatchewan, June 18 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an option that exists for its use, but is rarely effective.\par \par \uc2 "We are of the view that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in and of itself without policy action consistent with the direction of that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rarely effective in the long term. But it is an option that always exists," \uc2 Governor Mark Carney\uc2  told reporters.\par \par \uc2 He also reaffirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has an inflation-targeting mandate, believes in the floating exchange rate regime. (Reporting by Rod Nickel, writing by Ka Yan Ng; editing by Peter Galloway)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CANADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/CARNEY-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|CANT|ABN|D|E|U|RBN|M|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090618e56i001j4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
