\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:BOC Carney:Fundamentals Can't Account For C$ Volatility   \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2007\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with more details.)   \par \par \uc2 OTTAWA (Dow Jones)--Mark Carney, the incoming governor of the  \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 , Wednesday said fundamental factors can't account for the volatility of the Canadian dollar in recent months.   \par \par \uc2 He made the remarks in an unprecedented appearance before the House of Commons finance committee. It's the first time a governor designate has testified before the committee prior to formally assuming the post.   \par \par \uc2 Carney, who is currently adviser to Governor David Dodge, also said he doesn't favor pegging the Canadian dollar to the U.S. unit, or a monetary union. He said the  \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  must focus on inflation targeting in conducting monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 Carney also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to manage the Canadian dollar since 1998. The Bank only does so under exceptional circumstances. He said any decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  is made jointly with \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's department of finance.   \par \par \uc2 Carney said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarter-point rate cut Tuesday, the first since April 2004, has made the yield curve less steep.   \par \par \uc2 He said the Bank is trying to ensure that issues in the financial system doesn't spill over into the broad economy.   \par \par \uc2 Carney becomes governor Feb. 1 after Dodge retires Jan. 31.   \par \par \uc2 -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 613-237-0668; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com [ 12-05-0