\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE:Cda To Tell G20 C$ Bearing Brunt Of US$ Weakness-Official   \b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2007\par 16:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with more details.)   \par \par \uc2 OTTAWA (Dow Jones)--Canada has borne the brunt of the U.S. dollar's adjustment as the latter weakens against global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a senior Canadian finance official said Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 That is one of the key messages that Finance Minister Jim Flaherty will deliver to his G-20 counterparts and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors when they meet in Cape Town, South Africa this weekend, the official said at a briefing, speaking on condition of anonymity.   \par \par \uc2 He said the Canadian dollar and the euro have each accounted for about one-third of the U.S. dollar's effective depreciation. But Canada has been bearing a disproportionate share as its about one-10th the size of the euro area.   \par \par \uc2 The official refused to speculate on whether the G20 will discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself has no need for a targeted level of exchange rate and will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the most exceptional circumstances, he said.   \par \par \uc2 He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been doing its part to stimulate domestic demand as the U.S. economy slows, but other countries, notably China, haven't been doing their fair share.   \par \par \uc2 He said China needs to take greater steps to make its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexible to encourage domestic demand and rely less on exports. But while China has taken some small steps, they haven't been enough, as evidenced by its growing current account surplus. The U.S. deficit, meanwhile, remains huge and is likely to remain so for some time, the official said.   \par \par \uc2 He said the risks of global imbalances have increased. The G20 is a good forum for countries to have informal and frank discussions about the role they have to play to make adjustments work better for the global economy, he said.   \par \par \uc2 The key issue is about sharing the burden of adjustments to ensure they take place in a more orderly way with less volatility, he added.   \par \par \uc2 The G20 ministers will also discuss high energy prices, which are a challenge for many countries. They will also discuss the need for sovereign wealth funds to be more accountable and transparent.   \par \par \uc2 Flaherty will hold bilateral meetings with U.S. Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson, Mexican Finance Minister Agustin Carstens and U.K. Chancellor of the Exchequer Alistair Darling.   \par \par \uc2 -Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 613-237-0668; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com [ 11-13-07 1038ET ]   \par \par \uc2 4342   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020071113e3bd000al\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
