\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX -  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  powers of G7 countries   \b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2007\par 17:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 July 13 (Reuters) - France wants euro-zone politicians to have a stronger say over the value of the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 European treaties and agreements have left somewhat fuzzy the exact responsibilities for who controls \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, giving some leeway for French President Nicolas Sarkozy to press his case.   \par \par \uc2 The broad outlines however are clear -- it is a joint task of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministers, price stability must be the paramount concern, and while finance ministers can give general directions, the ECB decides upon actually conducting \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Below is a look at how the euro zone and other Group of Seven countries manage their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.   \par \par \uc2 EURO ZONE   \par \par \uc2 Decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy are a shared responsibility of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and European Union finance ministers. Like ECB monetary policy, the primary objective of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is to maintain price stability. Secondarily, the purpose is to support economic growth, as long as this does not conflict with the price stability objective.   \par \par \uc2 Finance ministers, with advice from the ECB, can reach agreements on an exchange rate system -- as they do in agreeing to admitting new members to the euro zone. They also can give general directions on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, although EU leaders have agreed only to exercise these powers in exceptional circumstances and without threatening ECB independence.   \par \par \uc2 The ECB has the sole competence for carrying out \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Nothing specifies that they require advance approval from EU finance ministers, although in practice it may consult them. It has its own \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and can call upon additional reserves held by member state central banks.   \par \par \uc2 No single European policymaker represents the euro in international fora. Group of Seven meetings are attended by finance ministers and central bankers from member countries France, Germany and Italy. ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet also attends with Luxembourg Prime Minister Jean-Claude Juncker, who represents the Eurogroup of euro-zone finance ministers. European Commissioner for Economic and Monetary Affairs Joaquin Almunia also attends some sessions.   \par \par \uc2 The ECB, in coordination with other G7 central banks, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late 2000 to support the value of the euro.   \par \par \uc2 For factbox on treaties, please click on [ID:nL13739517]   \par \par \uc2 UNITED STATES   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Treasury has primary responsibility for international financial policy and the U.S. Treasury Secretary speaks for the U.S. dollar. In practice, decisions on U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy are made in consultation with the Federal Reserve. Occassionally, they decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to counter disorderly market conditions. They use foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  equally from the reserves held at the Fed and from Treasury's Exchange Stabilisation Fund.   \par \par \uc2 JAPAN   \par \par \uc2 Japanese law requires that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  "shall endeavour to stabilise the external value of the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade and other measures". The MOF has regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although not recently. When markets are considered too volatile, MOF gives the Bank of Japan explicit directions on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- the amount, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs and the method. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts as its agent implementing the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. UNITED KINGDOM   \par \par \uc2 The Chancellor of the Exchequer is responsible for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and controls most of the UK's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. The Bank of England has the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but only for monetary policy purposes.   \par \par \uc2 UK policymakers have avoided making any explicit reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  management since the debacle in 1992 when sterling was forced out of the Exchange Rate Mechanism. They did, however, take part in the G7 coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the value of the euro in 2000.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CANADA\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The government establishes an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in close consultation with the  \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a discretionary basis, and currently acts only in the most exceptional circumstances. The bank has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since 1998 during the Asian crisis. Signs of a serious near-term market breakdown or the risk of extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements that seriously threaten sustainable long-term economic growth in \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be conditions that could warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The  \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducts the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as agent for the government, using reserves held in the government's Exchange Fund Account.   \par \par \uc2 EURO-POWERS/G7 (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070713e37d001ge\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
