\par\par \b \uc2 Canada dlr to hit parity with USD by end '07-CIBC   \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2007\par 14:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TORONTO, June 1 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar will reach parity with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the end of 2007 with the help of high commodity prices, ongoing merger-related interest and higher interest rates, CIBC World Markets said on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 CIBC said the Canadian dollar, which was last at par with the U.S. dollar in November 1976, will maintain parity with the greenback into at least the first quarter of 2008.   \par \par \uc2 "Between red-hot commodity and energy markets and huge capital inflows associated with an avalanche of M&A deals, the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has plenty of octane left to take a concerted run toward parity against the greenback," CIBC World Markets chief economist Jeff Rubin, said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 Rubin also said he does not expect the  \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a rising Canadian dollar and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would actually welcome a higher domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "With the national jobless rate plumbing 30-year lows and core inflation now bobbing above the  \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's target range, our earlier assumption of the  \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a further rise in the Canadian dollar with rate cuts, no longer seems tenable," Rubin said.   \par \par \uc2 According to Rubin, the Canadian dollar will also benefit from expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve to cut its key lending rate in the fourth quarter of 2007.   \par \par \uc2 At 8:35 a.m. (1235 GMT) the Canadian dollar was at C$1.0655 to the U.S. dollar, or 93.85 U.S. cents, which marked its highest level since July 1977.   \par \par \uc2 CANADA-DOLLAR-CIBC|LANGEN|ABN|E|U|RBN|CANT|D|M|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070601e36100137\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
