\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Of Canada Has No Specific Tgt For C$, Says Dodge   \b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2007\par 14:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 OTTAWA (Dow Jones)--Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have a specific target for the local dollar because it believes the value should be determined by market forces, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor David Dodge said Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998, Dodge said in a speech that he will deliver shortly to the ACI-The Financial Markets Association in Montreal.   \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Canada today still has no specific target for the dollar, because we believe that market conditions should determine the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value," he said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are restricted to "exceptional circumstances."   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the Canadian dollar since 1998," Dodge said. "A flexible exchange rate is crucial if a country is to pursue an independent monetary policy aimed at price stability."   \par \par \uc2 The text of his speech was released early under embargo to reporters in Ottawa.   \par \par \uc2 Web site:   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bankofcanada.ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bankofcanada.ca  }}}\uc2  [ 05-04-07 0902ET ]   \par \par \uc2 Bank of Canada Governor David Dodge touted Canada's success with a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though he acknowledged it can be hard for businesses to deal with big moves such as the Canadian dollar's 35% gain since early 2003.   \par \par \uc2 "But a fixed exchange rate is no panacea," he said. It can heighten uncertainty and add to volatility over time and limits how central bankers act because monetary policy must be aimed at protecting the fixed exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 Dodge said it's important for Canada to maintain its flexible exchange rate rather than peg the Canadian dollar to the U.S. unit. Although the U.S. is Canada's biggest trading partner, the structures of the two economies are different and often require different adjustments and different polices in reaction to shocks.   \par \par \uc2 "Canada's floating exchange rate facilitates these adjustments without forcing our economy through some very difficult changes in the overall level of output, wages, and prices," Dodge said.   \par \par \uc2 A fixed exchange rate can be the right choice for small economies where it's difficult to have an independent monetary policy, he said.   \par \par \uc2 "For systemically important countries, we should be promoting floating rates supported by well-developed and well-functioning domestic financial markets," he said.   \par \par \uc2 However, until such well-developed markets are in place, these economies may need to manage capital flows and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets   \par \par \uc2 "These capital controls and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are awkward, and over time, they can lead to a lot of problems. So they must be eliminated as quickly as possible," Dodge said.   \par \par \uc2 But to the extent they are making progress, Canada and other developed economies must tolerate such awkwardness, he added.   \par \par \uc2 -Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 613-237-0668; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com [ 05-04-07 0910ET ]   \par \par \uc2 4346   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020070504e3540007e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
