\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-BoC moves to talk down C$ with statement  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Cameron French  \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 20:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TORONTO, March 7 (Reuters) - The wording of the Bank of Canada's statement on Tuesday shows it's concerned about the Canadian dollar's push to 14-year highs, but the bank is opting to try to talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down, rather than resorting to the last-ditch tool of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 After raising its overnight interest rate to 3.75 percent from 3.50 percent, the bank suggested its current tightening cycle may be drawing to a close, and noted the Canadian dollar has risen more than it had expected in its most recent economic assessment.  \par \par \uc2 The weight of the two points prompted traders to unwind Canadian dollar bets which had factored in one or two more rate hikes over the next two meetings.  \par \par \uc2 It also calmed some muted market speculation that the bank might take direct market action to rein in the loonie, which hit 14-year highs last week.  \par \par \uc2 "The fact that the dollar was even raised in the statement, I think at the very least, suggests the bank is keeping a close eye on it," said Doug Porter, deputy chief economist at BMO Nesbitt Burns.  \par \par \uc2 The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened 11 percent over the past 10 months against the U.S. dollar, propped up by rising interest rates, surging commodity prices and foreign takeover interest in Canadian companies.  \par \par \uc2 However, the most recent advance has come despite doubts about how aggressively the Bank of Canada plans to raise rates, and with less support from oil and gas prices which have eased from recent highs.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say this has fueled worries at the bank that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise has been in part driven not by economic fundamentals, but by investors betting on its continued momentum.  \par \par \uc2 "The idea in the marketplace that (the Canadian dollar) is a one-way trade is possibly drawing unwanted investor attention with potential implications affecting the fabric of an economy in the midst of a resource reallocation process," said HSBC \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Stewart Hall in an e-mailed comment.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?  \par \par \uc2 This prompted some to wonder last week whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might take the ultimate step and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- or sell Canadian dollars on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to depress the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- if it continued to push higher.  \par \par \uc2 Serious talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last swirled in 2002 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was stagnating around 62 U.S. cents.  \par \par \uc2 But the bank has not actually taken the step since 1998, when it changed its policy to allow for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exceptional circumstances.  \par \par \uc2 Despite hefty layoffs in the manufacturing sector and speculation about a 90-cent loonie, analysts don't believe the situation warrants such drastic action.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think it's the sky-is-falling scenario just yet," said George Davis, chief technical strategist at RBC Capital Markets.  \par \par \uc2 He said that if economic data began to weaken alongside a rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of Canada might take action, but by altering monetary policy rather than by direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 One Toronto-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been much more transparent in its actions in recent years, and would clearly telegraph an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it was thinking of it.  \par \par \uc2 However, given the sharpness of the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move following the bank's statement, any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns will likely be shelved for the time being.  \par \par \uc2 By mid-afternoon, the loonie was at C$1.1493 to the U.S. dollar, or 87.01 U.S. cents, about 1-1/2 U.S. cents below last week's highs.  \par \par \uc2 "We've seen how the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reacts today just to a very slight toning-down on the 'hawk-o-meter,' so there's a lot the bank can do before they resort to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said BMO Nesbitt's Porter. (Additional reporting by Amran Abocar)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 CANADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|CANT  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060310e237001rq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw202\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3030\pichgoal600
