\par\par \b \uc2 GATA: European  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Gold Sales Repeatedly Cap Price around $440  \b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2005\par 16:54\par \uc2 Business Wire\par \uc2 BWR\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005  Business Wire. All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 DALLAS - (BUSINESS WIRE) - July 7, 2005 - The price of gold has been capped at $440 per ounce since last December by repeated selling of gold reserves by European central banks and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself, the Gold Anti-Trust Action Committee disclosed today.  \par \par \uc2 GATA's finding was based on the research of its consultant, gold market expert John Brimelow of Aegis Capital in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "The ECB reported on Wednesday a sale of 360 million euros in gold last week, 996,592 ounces at the bank's new book value for gold, or 31 tonnes," Brimelow said today. "This is a huge amount, matched only by the sale of 47 tonnes announced at the end of March (but reported only in May) and a 31.9-tonnes sale last December last year."  \par \par \uc2 Each of these sales corresponded with gold's penetration of the $440 price level, as can been seen at the one-year gold price chart here:  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.kitco.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.kitco.com/ }}}\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "An indisputable pattern has now developed for the ECB to step forward as a massive seller when gold approaches the $440s," Brimelow said. "Curiously, the euro price of gold does not seem to be as sensitive an issue with the ECB."  \par \par \uc2 The massive selling of gold in recent months by European central banks, Brimelow added, suggests that they will be obliged to suspend sales in September if they are to keep within the volume limits they set for themselves in the renewal of the Washington Agreement on Gold.  \par \par \uc2 The latest ECB gold sales were shown on the bank's consolidated financial report for July 1, posted this week on the Internet here:  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ecb.de/press/pr/wfs/2005/html/fs050706.en.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.ecb.de/press/pr/wfs/2005/html/fs050706.en.html }}}\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Brimelow's research echoed comments made Tuesday by John Embry, chief investment strategist for Sprott Asset Management of Toronto, during an interview with Report on Business Television in Canada. Embry, who will speak at GATA's Gold Rush 21 conference in Dawson City, Yukon Territory, \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , from August 7 to 9, likened the current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of central banks against the gold price to their coordinated selling of gold in the 1960s via what was called the London Gold Pool. Embry noted that market demand for bullion eventually overwhelmed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplies then and he predicted a similar outcome soon.  \par \par \uc2 GATA Chairman Bill Murphy today repeated the organization's belief that, because of their sales and leasing of gold and their false accounting of leased gold as gold still in the vault, central banks possess only a fraction of the gold they claim to have. Murphy added that the purpose of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gold sales and leasing is not really what is represented by the banks -- to raise money from a "dead asset" -- but rather to manipulate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and precious metals markets and deceive them about reckless government monetary policies.  \par \par \uc2 Gold Anti-Trust Action Committee, Dallas Bill Murphy, 214-522-3411  \par \par \uc2 Dokument BWR0000020050707e177005pm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
