\par\par \b \uc2 Bush says yuan unfair, yen to be issue at G7.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Alan Wheatley  \par \uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  PHUKET, Thailand, Sept 5 (Reuters) - U.S. President George W. Bush said that Beijing's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg was unfair while \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its yen would be discussed at this month's Group of Seven meeting.   \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has become a thorny political issue following U.S. calls, carried by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow to Tokyo and Beijing this week, for Asia to allow its heavily protected \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise.   \par \par \uc2  Following inconclusive talks between Snow and Chinese policymakers in Beijing on whether the yuan should be allowed to appreciate, Bush said Washington would "deal with it accordingly".   \par \par \uc2  In a CNBC interview, Bush said Snow used meetings in Beijing to "deliver a strong message from the administration that we expect our trading partners to treat our people fairly - our producers and workers and farmers and manufacturers - and we don't think we're being treated fairly when a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is controlled by the government."   \par \par \uc2  U.S. patience with Japan's ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the strengthening yen also appears to be wearing thin.   \par \par \uc2  Canadian Finance Minister John Manley told Reuters that Snow would be keen to discuss Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at this month's meeting of leading industrialised countries in Dubai.   \par \par \uc2  "I think he'll want to talk about the Japanese. We know that one of the purposes of his trip to Japan was to include some discussion on that," said Manley, who, like Snow, is in Phuket for an Asia-Pacific finance ministers' meeting.   \par \par \uc2  DETERMINED \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Dealers reported determined \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan on Thursday to prevent the yen from approaching the key level of 115 to the dollar. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent nearly $80 billion this year, a record, to brake the yen's rise.   \par \par \uc2  Manley's comments pushed the yen higher in late morning trade but gains were capped on concern that the Japanese would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the yen rose too far. At 0300 GMT the dollar was at 116.81.   \par \par \uc2  The latest round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came just days after Snow left Tokyo, his first stop on a regional tour seen by many analysts as a bid to respond to claims by U.S. manufacturers that Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies make the region's exports unfairly cheap.   \par \par \uc2  The Bush administration is under domestic pressure to stem the loss of U.S. manufacturing jobs in the run-up to the 2004 presidential election. Manufacturing is an important political and fund-raising base for the president.   \par \par \uc2  Snow has been less critical of Japan than China in recent months, despite massive Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , possibly reflecting a Washington view that a fragile Japanese economic recovery could be derailed by a stronger yen, economists say.   \par \par \uc2  JAPAN MUM   \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, declined to comment on Friday on whether authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market a day earlier, saying only that the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was unchanged.   \par \par \uc2  "I have no comment, but there is no change to our stance," Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs and the leader of Japan's delegation at the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) meeting in Phuket, Thailand, told reporters.   \par \par \uc2  Asia has a mix of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes. China and Malaysia peg their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar, while some others float their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically to prevent destabilising lurches.   \par \par \uc2  The dispute over the yuan is not expected to result in trade sanctions, partly because around half of China's exports come from foreign firms operating there that take advantage of cheap labour to produce shipments of everything from computer keyboards to toys.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030905dz95000nl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
