\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar drops for fourth day, bonds mixed. \b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2002\par 23:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  Bank of Canada: CANADA OPEN 1.6023 PREVIOUS CLOSE 1.5978 - \par \par \uc2  By Ka Yan Ng \par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Feb 6 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar dropped through the psychologically key C$1.60 level on Wednesday to end lower for a fourth day in a row. \par \par \uc2  Canadian bonds also fell as new supply met with soft demand. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar ended at C$1.6047 to the U.S. dollar, or 62.32 U.S. cents, down from C$1.5973 to the U.S. dollar, or 62.61 U.S. cents, at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  "Frankly, I didn't think the recent rally that we got was going to be sustainable in any event," said Marc Levesque, senior economist at Toronto-Dominion Bank. \par \par \uc2  Four days of declines have pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward its record low and have almost unwound all the gains the fragile Canadian dollar made after Canadian officials began a campaign of talking up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  three weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  "(Canadian officials) may have talked up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tried to convince people it should be stronger than it is, but they haven't backed up their words with anything more concrete than that," said Levesque. \par \par \uc2  On the backburner is the threat that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But most observers do not see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  coming in around C$1.60. Recent data showed Canadian foreign reserve holdings were US$33.64 billion for January. \par \par \uc2  In economic news, the Canadian help-wanted data for January suggested the year-long decline in labor demand is stabilizing, while building permits for December fell. In the United States, a report suggested solid economic recovery as the productivity of U.S. workers grew at a brisker-than-expected pace in the fourth quarter of 2001. \par \par \uc2  CANADIAN BONDS MIXED, LONG END LAGS AFTER AUCTIONS \par \par \uc2  Canadian bonds started in positive territory on Wednesday, and ended mixed. Long-dated maturities lagged because of poor demand for 10-year notes after an auction by Canadian and U.S. governments. \par \par \uc2  "Supply is knocking the market back and today's 10-year auction results reflected lackluster interest," said Rob Palombi, senior fixed income analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Treasury sale of $13 billion in 10-year notes produced poor results because of fears of higher interest rates later in the year and dealers dumped inventory once the results were known. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada's 10-year bond auction resulted in an average yield of 5.397 percent at an average price of C$98.842. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 10-year bond shed 15 Canadian cents to C$104.88 to yield 5.326 percent. The U.S. 10-year Treasury was down 8/32 to yield 4.929 percent. \par \par \uc2  Despite weakness in the stock markets, bonds couldn't convincingly pull themselves from the negative column as concerns about accounting practices still had a hold on the market. \par \par \uc2  The two-year bond gained 1 Canadian cent to C$103.22 to yield 3.154 percent. The yield spread between the two-year and 10-year bond moved to 217.2 basis points from 214.5 basis points at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  The 30-year bond, due 2029, dropped 30 Canadian cents to C$101.70 to yield 5.627 percent. \par \par \uc2  The three-month when-issued T-bill yielded 1.99 percent, unchanged from the previous close. \par \par \uc2  ($1=$1.60 Canadian). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020206dy26016g8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
