\par\par \b \uc2  Aussie slips to one-month low vs yen, greenback. \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2002\par 11:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 30 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar slipped to a one-month low against the yen on Wednesday on expectation of repatriation of funds by Japanese investors ahead of their fiscal year-end book closings. \par \par \uc2  That in turn pushed the Aussie down to a one-month low against the dollar with investors focused on a key interest rate decision by the Federal Reserve later in the session. \par \par \uc2  "(Fed chairman Alan) Greenspan's statement is the key. If we have more signs of a U.S. recovery the Aussie can do better but at the moment the move in the cross is impacting the Aussie more than anything else," said Jane Foley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  The Fed is expected to leave its fed funds rate unchanged at 1.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  By 1030 GMT the Aussie stood at 67.06 yen , off its 23-week high of 70.14 set late last week. Against the dollar, it lost nearly two thirds of a percent on the day to stand at US$0.5061 . \par \par \uc2  The Aussie has been on a steep uptrend against a generally weak yen since late September partly because Japanese investors have been buying Australian bonds to seek higher yields, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But Japanese investors are expected to repatriate their funds ahead of their fiscal year-end book closings in March to boost their balance sheets. \par \par \uc2  "... if Japanese repatriation continues then the cross may continue to be sold aggressively to the detriment of the Aussie against the U.S. dollar as well," UBS Warburg said in a note to clients. The New Zealand dollar fell against the U.S. dollar in sympathy with the Aussie. It stood at US$0.4148 from levels just above $0.42 on Tuesday. The Canadian dollar stood at C$1.5877 , pulling itself off its one-month high set on Tuesday against the greenback as investors took profits ahead of a rate decision by the Fed. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained sharply in the previous session, drawing support from comments made earlier this week by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor David Dodge that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is a tool in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's toolbox. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020130dy1u00lrv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
