\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Dlr Seen Benefiting From Perceived Policy Shift \b0\par\par\uc2  By Don Curren \par \uc2 942 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2002\par 19:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TORONTO -(Dow Jones)- The veiled threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a nervous \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market combined to inject a burst of strength in the anemic Canadian dollar Tuesday, but there's no guarantee the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vigor will be sustained, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Beginning with a sharp improvement late Monday, the Canadian dollar rocketed higher Tuesday as market players scrambled to get out of short positions in the embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's definitely been the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice today," said Tim Mazanec, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Investors Bank & Trust in Boston. \par \par \uc2  "Right now, the new trend is for a stronger Canadian (dollar). We'll have to see if momentum players push that strength even further," he added. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar, which reached an all-time high of C$1.6194 on Jan. 21, tumbled almost 200 points from its Monday close of C$1.6027 to an intraday low of C$1.5841 on Tuesday before recovering substantially in busy trading. \par \par \uc2  It was at C$1.5903 in early afternoon trading. \par \par \uc2  While a mass exodus from short Canadian dollar positions was seen as a primary cause for the move, analysts said another round of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor David Dodge - along with the implicit threat of direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - likely played a role. \par \par \uc2  Repeating comments initially made last Wednesday, Dodge said in a speech Monday that the Canadian dollar's recent weakness was "not helpful" for the Canadian economy and that economic recovery in Canada "does not hinge on the current low levels of the Canadian dollar against its U.S. counterparts." \par \par \uc2  He repeated the comments again in a separate speech on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dodge also referred to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as one of the tools available to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, but since then has not elaborated on the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or any other aspects of it. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    STOPPING SHORT OF A "STRONG DOLLAR POLICY"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However cautious the remarks from Dodge and Finance Minister Paul\par Martin might be, they are seen by many analysts as a decisive shift away\par from the implicit sanctioning of a lower \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that seemed to emanate\par from Ottawa in the past.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is a clear sign that there has been a potential policy shift\par away from the perception that the government wants a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par boost exports and toward something more supportive," said a report from\par John Johnston, chief economist for the Americas at RBC Capital Markets\par in Toronto.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "However, the government has stopped short of a 'strong dollar policy'\par along the lines of the U.S. strong dollar policy and its is unlikely to\par announce any major change in macroeconomic policy designed to\par specifically support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," the report said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Ottawa's move does constitute a serious policy shift, and changes\par the impact of politics on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from negative to neutral, the\par report said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Benjamin Tal, senior economist at the Canadian Imperial Bank of\par Commerce, said the verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Canadian officials helped\par buttress the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by inducing fear of market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  among\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Clearly, yesterday we saw some technical factors," he said. "But in\par the background, the verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and\par (Finance Minister Paul Martin) clearly helped."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With about $34 billion in the bank's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, the\par threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is taken seriously by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market players,\par Tal said. "Clearly, fear regarding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the main factor here\par - it's not the fundamentals," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  starts selling off again, market players may begin to\par test the bank's resolve and its willingness to actually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "At one point the Bank of Canada will have to deliver in order to\par support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . You cannot support this kind of equilibrium where\par the bank talks, and the market reacts, without seeing any action," Tal\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "You can't just be saying stuff like that, and not backing it up,"\par Investors Trust's Mazanec said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar could test as low as C$1.5820, but is likely to head\par back up to the C$1.6110 area, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If current levels prove unsustainable and the U.S. dollar climbs back\par to C$1.6130 (a Canadian dollar level of $0.62), the bank may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par Tal said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On other hand, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent strength may create an opportune\par time for the bank to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he added. "I would not surprised if the\par Bank of Canada would take advantage of the current improved sentiment -\par at least temporarily improved sentiment - and give it an extra push," he\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Tal and other analysts suggest another option for the bank is to\par wait for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to reach its natural low and then start improving\par as the economy improves. The bank may use that opportunity to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to support its natural appreciation, Tal said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He puts the probability of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at no more than 50%, and adds\par that any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would likely be coordinated with the U.S. Federal\par Reserve. "We definitely need the Fed on our side on this one. The Bank\par of Canada cannot do it by itself," Tal said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RBC's Johnston suggested in his report that the probability of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains fairly low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Mr. Dodge hinted last week that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a\par possibility, though we believe that the BOC will only use this tool if\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were to weaken substantially in very disorderly markets,"\par the report said.\par    -By Don Curren, Dow Jones Newswires; 416-306-2020;\par don.curren@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020129dy1t009ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
