\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar rallies after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  warning. \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2002\par 12:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar remained firm on Tuesday, extending sharp gains against its U.S. counterpart made in Asia and in the previous session as Canadian officials continued to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor David Dodge repeated on Monday his warning that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is a tool in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's toolbox. In recent days, the finance minister and even the prime minister have also been supporting their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which hit record lows last week, with their words. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the loonie, as the Canadian dollar is known, also drew support from news on Monday that British energy retailer Centrica Plc is buying the home heating serrvices arm of Canada's Enbridge Inc for C$1 billion. \par \par \uc2  "We've had quite a move. The Centrica M&A deal was Canada positive," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  At 1113 GMT, the Canadian dollar was trading around C$1.5907 per dollar compared with the previous day's Bank of Canada official closing rate of C$1.5976 (at 2230 GMT) and levels around C$1.6120 earlier earlier on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said some retracement of the Canadian dollar had been inevitable as the latest IMM data (as at January 22) indicated that non-commercial net-short positions in the loonie were at their highest level since November 27, 2001. \par \par \uc2  "It seems the world and his wife had been shorting Canada and people started pulling out," said a trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Canada's December composite index is due for release at 1330 GMT but of more interest will be November's gross domestic prooduct report on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Australian dollar was weaker against its U.S. counterpart in line with the euro's weakness against the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "The Australian is lower because of the weakness of the euro even though we've had some good data," said Fornasari. \par \par \uc2  National Australia Bank's December business conditions rose two points to above its pre-September 11 levels at four points. Even more encouraging was a leap in business confidence to 13.6 points from 4.5 points in November. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020129dy1t00ngk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
