\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar zooms up after more verbal support. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ka Yan Ng \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2002\par 23:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Jan 28 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar swooped \par \par \uc2  higher on Monday as officials launched another round of verbal \par \par \uc2  support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it still faces pressure if \par \par \uc2  figures to be released this week show credible signs of U.S. \par \par \uc2  economic stability. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , mired around C$1.61 to the U.S dollar for \par \par \uc2  much of the overnight session, zoomed higher on more words from \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Paul Martin, Bank of Canada Governor David \par \par \uc2  Dodge, and Prime Minister Jean Chretien. \par \par \uc2      The Canadian dollar ended at C$1.6027 to the U.S. dollar, \par \par \uc2  or 62.39 U.S. cents, up sharply from C$1.6104 to the U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar, or 62.10 U.S. cents. \par \par \uc2      The Canadian unit continued to rise after the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Canada published its official closing rate. At 5:30 p.m. (2230 \par \par \uc2  GMT), the Canadian dollar was at C$1.5976 per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2      It received short-lived support from kind words last week, \par \par \uc2  but a second round of government defense in as many weeks \par \par \uc2  caught the market's attention on Monday. \par \par \uc2      "Being that it was the third or fourth verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  the market is starting to take notice of it," said Paul Briggs, \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Investors Bank and Trust in Boston. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       The three officials had made various attempts last week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and came out with a renewed and spirited defense on Monday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par declaring the dollar weakness to be unhelpful and unjustified\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by Canada's economic fundamentals and by signs of a pickup, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par all the officials stopped short of promising any immediate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par action to come to its aid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor David Dodge said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still a tool in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's arsenal but would not be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par drawn on whether it would be used to support the faltering\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The issue basically comes down to the double-edged comment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that not only was the falling Canadian dollar not necessary to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par produce a recovery, but that it was undesirable," said Andrew\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Pyle, senior financial markets analyst at Scotia Capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "That still leaves us with the questions of if, when and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par how much will the bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to reinforce the line in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sand on (the Canadian dollar), but it is clear that interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates cannot be used until stronger signs from the economy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par emerge."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He noted that Monday's gains may be used as an opportunity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to sell the Canadian unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     UPSIDE MOMENTUM NOW, BUT RISKS PRESSURE FROM U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Other analysts said if the Canadian dollar could break\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par through the next key level of C$1.5980, it could provide some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par extra momentum to the rally. Failing that, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be headed back to its record low of C$1.6194.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risks further weakness in a week that is heavy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with economic news. The Fed's policy-setting arm will start its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-day meeting on Tuesday, and is expected to stand pat on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates at the conclusion of its meeting on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Apart from the Fed's rate decision, a barrage of U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic news is expected this week, including payrolls,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consumer sentiment, and the Institute for Supply Management's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par manufacturing survey.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The numbers that are coming out this week are probably\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par going to confirm stability in the U.S. economy, that should do\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nothing other than...see the Canadian dollar weaken off,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said Jack Spitz, regional manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par National Bank of Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Canadian economics calendar is fairly light,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highlighted by the November gross domestic product report for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In cross-trading, the Canadian dollar         was at 83.39\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen versus 83.46 yen at the previous close. Against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Australian dollar , it was at A$1.2105 compared with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A$1.2015 at the previous close. Against the euro , the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canadian dollar was at C$1.3780 versus C$1.3919 at the previous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020128dy1s016ln\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
