\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Of Canada's Dodge: Recent C$ Slump 'Not Helpful' \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2002\par 17:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones News Service \par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OTTAWA -(Dow Jones)- At a press conference Wednesday, Bank of Canada Governor David Dodge said the recent devaluation of the Canadian dollar is "not helpful" to the country's economic recovery and raises questions of confidence in the overall economy. \par \par \uc2  Dodge agreed with earlier comments made by Canadian Finance Minister Paul Martin that Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been hurt, in part, by a perception problem and that the current value of the dollar doesn't reflect the underlying fundamentals of the Canadian economy. \par \par \uc2  Canada's dollar recently closed at a record low of 62.02 U.S. cents, though it has since risen slightly. \par \par \uc2  Dodge went on to say that recent economic indicators have shown that Canada's economy is stronger than had been anticipated, with exports rising, the manufacturing sector lowering inventories and receiving new orders, factory orders and retail sales rising, and household spending more robust than expected. Dodge said that, over time, this positive economic news should be reflected in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "As I've always said, the best medicine for the dollar is a strong economy," Dodge said. \par \par \uc2  Dodge reiterated the Bank of Canada's assessment that the Canadian economy will start slowly this year, but that economic growth should steadily gain momentum throughout the year and finish 2002 with annualized growth between 3% and 4%. \par \par \uc2  "There's much more certainty today than there was three months ago that a recovery will be well underway" by year-end, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dodge said the Canadian economy, which has been slowing since the middle of 2001, is now at a "turning point." However, he stressed that a degree of uncertainty remains in the outlook, mainly that business confidence in North America still remains weak, though it should rebound later this year. \par \par \uc2  Dodge wouldn't say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would consider a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "That is a tool in our tool chest," the governor said, refusing to comment further on the likely hood of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -Joel Baglole, Dow Jones Newswires; 613-237-0668 \par \par \uc2  4217 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020020123dy1n001k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
