\par\par \b \uc2  Canada  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  speaks out in dollar defense. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Amran Abocar \par \uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2002\par 21:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Jan 23 (Reuters) - Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied to the defense of the dollar on Wednesday, boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's short-term prospects as markets pondered the possibility of tougher measures, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In unusually direct comments, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor David Dodge said the Canadian dollar's decline was a source of concern, and its depreciation was not helpful because it raised issues of confidence. \par \par \uc2  He was the second Canadian official to defend the dollar this week - Finance Minister Paul Martin spoke out on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped to record lows. \par \par \uc2  "Dodge has put the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on alert although he's basically given a stay of execution," said Rob Palombi, senior analyst at Standard & Poor's. "The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is real. It's up to the market now and it sounds like the Bank of Canada is going to give it some time to digest all the improving economic news. \par \par \uc2  "If at that point, the Canadian dollar continues to depreciate, that's when we might see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to support the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for several years, although it admits \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be part of its arsenal. \par \par \uc2  "It's always a tool in our tool chest but you wouldn't expect me to come before you and say if we would use it, when we would use it or how much we would do," Dodge said on Wednesday. "So since you wouldn't expect it I won't give you the answer." \par \par \uc2  On Monday Martin stopped the sliding dollar in its tracks when he signaled his displeasure with its weakness and said markets were ignoring Canada's strong fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  RETHINKING DOLLAR VIEWS \par \par \uc2  Startled market players, unaccustomed to policymakers expressing such spirited concern about the exchange rate, began to reconsider their view on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Whether the verbal support alone can really accomplish anything for more than a week is up for debate," said Doug Porter, senior economist at BMO Nesbitt Burns. \par \par \uc2  "But the more stridently Ottawa tries to quash the sense that they favor a weaker dollar, I think that has a more positive effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ultimately." \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was at C$1.6020 on Wednesday afternoon, well above the record of C$1.6194 set Monday and slightly above the C$1.6060 level seen before Dodge began to speak. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the rescue missions should help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the very short term. But ultimately the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is linked to factors outside \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  control - a Canadian economic recovery that in turn hinges on an end to the recession in the United States, Canada's biggest trading partner. \par \par \uc2  Alan Ruskin, research director at 4Cast Ltd. in New York said strength in the Canadian dollar would come if there was a shift in sentiment toward the greenback, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice for safe-haven seekers. \par \par \uc2  "The idea that the economy will turn the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around has been tried, tested, and has failed," he said. "To see the Canadian dollar strengthen, you will more likely need to see a turn in (U.S.) dollar sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "And you will need a turn in euro sentiment, in particular, before you get that turn in the dollar sentiment." \par \par \uc2  Dodge would not be drawn on whether Ottawa would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but he didn't rule out the possibility either. \par \par \uc2  "He didn't count it out and I guess he wants to hold it over the markets head as a possibility if it weakens off dramatically or too quickly," said Ronald Pancer, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Societe Generale. "But he certainly didn't suggest that he was looking at it any time soon either." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has $34 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to support the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the Asian crisis, spending some $4 billion. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has slumped as the economy grapples with recession and a belief that Canada will lag a U.S. recovery. A modest interest rate cut by the Bank of Canada last week proved a disappointment for some people who had hoped for a heftier move to stimulate the economy. \par \par \uc2  (With additional reporting by New York financial desk) \par \par \uc2  ($1=$1.60 Canadian). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020123dy1n01377\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
