\par\par \b \uc2  Martin defense lifts Canada dollar after close. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Amran Abocar \par \uc2 706 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2002\par 00:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Jan 21 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar hit its \par \par \uc2  highest level of a dismal day after the close on Monday as \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Paul Martin said Canada was worried about the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stubborn decline. \par \par \uc2  At 5:25 p.m., the Canadian unit was trading at C$1.6102 to \par \par \uc2  the U.S dollar, or 62.10 U.S. cents, up from its closing level \par \par \uc2  of C$1.6115, or 62.05 U.S. cents, and well above the record of \par \par \uc2  C$1.6194, notched early in the day in European trade. \par \par \uc2  Martin said the government was "not happy" with the low \par \par \uc2  level of the dollar but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would eventually \par \par \uc2  reflect the country's good economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Martin said the market's perception of the Canadian economy \par \par \uc2  was not in sync with the reality, citing the balanced budget, a \par \par \uc2  falling debt-to-GDP ratio and a large current account surplus. \par \par \uc2  "If one thing stands out, it's the very flat statement that \par \par \uc2  the government is not happy with the falling Canadian dollar," \par \par \uc2  said Doug Porter, senior economist at BMO Nesbitt Burns. \par \par \uc2  "I think that was an important statement. Anything that \par \par \uc2  helps dispel the perception that Ottawa welcomes an ever \par \par \uc2  falling dollar is helpful at this point." \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar, which plumbed record depths against \par \par \uc2  the greenback in overnight trading, had recovered slightly to \par \par \uc2  end on a firmer note on Monday but dealers brushed aside the \par \par \uc2  gains and braced for more weakness. \par \par \uc2  Volumes were tepid during the session in the absence of \par \par \uc2  U.S. market players because of the Martin Luther King Day \par \par \uc2  holiday. \par \par \uc2  "It's just corporates taking advantage of a strong U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar and locking in some gains," said Reid Farrill, executive \par \par \uc2  director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at CIBC World Markets. "I wouldn't \par \par \uc2  confuse that with a Canadian dollar rally." \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped to a record low after \par \par \uc2  automatic sell orders were triggered in Europe, erasing the \par \par \uc2  previous record set only last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Steve Demers, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at National \par \par \uc2  Bank of Canada in Montreal, said the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be \par \par \uc2  stuck in "no man's land" as it groped around to establish firm \par \par \uc2  new lows and the market would have to rely on medium- to \par \par \uc2  long-term technical indicators for guidance. \par \par \uc2  Those indicators suggest C$1.6225 is a level at which the \par \par \uc2  Canadian dollar could hold against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a few \par \par \uc2  days. The Canadian dollar could potentially trade as low as \par \par \uc2  C$1.6500 to C$1.6600 level, Demers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SPECULATION \par \par \uc2  As the Canadian dollar slumps to one low after another, \par \par \uc2  talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become more \par \par \uc2  pronounced. \par \par \uc2  Considering the Canadian unit's orderly decline, the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not likely to step in unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loses \par \par \uc2  ground rapidly but that has not dampened speculation. \par \par \uc2  BMO Nesbitt Burns' Porter said Martin's comments could be \par \par \uc2  the prelude to a more aggressive stance. \par \par \uc2  "This is the first step. It might be laying the ground work \par \par \uc2  for some actions rather than words," Porter said. "But I think \par \par \uc2  it's obvious that policymakers aren't quite ready or aren't at \par \par \uc2  that stage yet." \par \par \uc2  Martin declined to be drawn on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  might step into \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to defend the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on so many minds, attention is riveted on \par \par \uc2  Bank of Canada Governor David Dodge who will present the \par \par \uc2  Monetary Policy Report Update on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, Canadian retail sales rose 1.4 percent in \par \par \uc2  November against October, driven by strong auto sector sales \par \par \uc2  prompted by zero-financing deals. Excluding autos, retail sales \par \par \uc2  fell 0.6 percent in November. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian unit, which opened at C$1.6175, moved in a \par \par \uc2  range of C$1.6110 to C$1.6184 during the session, according to \par \par \uc2  Reuters data and traders \par \par \uc2  In cross-trading, the Canadian dollar was at 82.22 \par \par \uc2  yen versus 82.19 yen at the previous close. Against the \par \par \uc2  Australian dollar , it was at A$1.1983, compared with \par \par \uc2  A$1.2031 at the previous close. Against the euro , the \par \par \uc2  Canadian dollar was at C$1.4237 versus C$1.4267 at the previous \par \par \uc2  close. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020122dy1l00014\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
