\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar sets new record, seen falling. \b0\par\par\uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2002\par 15:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      Reuters plans to combine coverage of the Canadian capital \par \par \uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets into one report that will have all \par \par \uc2  the usual features of both the Canadian dollar report and the \par \par \uc2  Canadian bond report. \par \par \uc2      The new report, which begins Feb. 4, will continue to be \par \par \uc2  delivered twice daily. It will be found on pages and \par \par \uc2  , the pages currently used for two separate reports. \par \par \uc2      If you have any comments, please contact Canadian Bureau \par \par \uc2  Chief Russell Blinch at russell.blinch@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2      Bank of Canada: CANADA OPEN  1.6138  PREVIOUS CLOSE 1.6096 \par \par \uc2  -------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Jan 21 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar, which \par \par \uc2  plumbed record depths against the greenback in overnight \par \par \uc2  trading, opened slightly firmer on Monday but was in clear \par \par \uc2  danger of dropping lower amid thin volumes. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped to new all-time lows in \par \par \uc2  overnight trading after automatic sell orders were triggered \par \par \uc2  around C$1.6170. That pushed the Canadian unit, which had set a \par \par \uc2  new historic low only last Thursday, down further to C$1.6194, \par \par \uc2  or 61.75 U.S. cents. \par \par \uc2  "This is a no man's land as we establish new all-time \par \par \uc2  lows," said Steve Demers, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \par \par \uc2  National Bank of Canada in Montreal. "It means we fall back on \par \par \uc2  some medium-to long-term technical indicators to guide us as \par \par \uc2  to where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could evolve. \par \par \uc2  "That's dominating the market right now. Liquidity is lower \par \par \uc2  and its dominated by speculators who are using technical \par \par \uc2  indicators." \par \par \uc2  Those indicators suggest C$1.6225 is a level at which the \par \par \uc2  Canadian dollar could hold against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a few \par \par \uc2  days. The Canadian dollar could potentially trade as low as \par \par \uc2  C$1.6500 to C$1.6600 level, Demers said. \par \par \uc2  "We've been in a bearish trend on the Canadian dollar since \par \par \uc2  July and this trend can only be broken by getting some good \par \par \uc2  volatility distribution," he said. "The trend lines are \par \par \uc2  suggesting C$1.65 before that happens." \par \par \uc2  At 9:30 a.m. (1430 GMT), the Canadian dollar was at \par \par \uc2  C$1.6158, or 61.89 U.S. cents. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at C$1.6175 \par \par \uc2  to the U.S. dollar, or 61.82 U.S. cents compared with C$1.6125, \par \par \uc2  or 62.02 U.S. cents, at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  With U.S. financial markets closed on Monday for the Martin \par \par \uc2  Luther King holiday, the thinner trading conditions contain the \par \par \uc2  risk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be led even lower. \par \par \uc2      In overseas action, the Canadian unit moved in a range of \par \par \uc2  C$1.6140 to C$1.6194, according to Reuters data and traders. \par \par \uc2      As the Canadian dollar slumps to one low after another, \par \par \uc2  talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become more \par \par \uc2  pronounced. \par \par \uc2      But considering the Canadian unit's orderly decline, the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not likely to step in unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loses \par \par \uc2  ground rapidly. \par \par \uc2      With \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on so many minds, attention is riveted on \par \par \uc2  Bank of Canada governor David Dodge who will present the \par \par \uc2  Monetary Policy Report Update on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      "There's a good chance that you don't get an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  before C$1.64, C$1.65 and only if the move to that level is \par \par \uc2  done in the next couple of weeks," Demers added. \par \par \uc2      On the economic front, Statistics Canada said domestic \par \par \uc2  retail sales rose 1.4 percent in November against October, \par \par \uc2  driven by strong auto sector sales prompted by zero-financing \par \par \uc2  deals. Excluding autos, retail sales fell 0.6 percent in \par \par \uc2  November. \par \par \uc2  In the previous session, the Canadian dollar ended weaker \par \par \uc2  after finding no support from healthy trade numbers that showed \par \par \uc2  a rebound in the country's exports. \par \par \uc2  In cross-trading, the Canadian dollar was at 81.92 \par \par \uc2  yen versus 82.19 yen at the previous close. Against the \par \par \uc2  Australian dollar , it was at A$1.1935 compared with \par \par \uc2  A$1.2031 at the previous close. Against the euro , the \par \par \uc2  Canadian dollar was at C$1.4292 versus C$1.4267 at the previous \par \par \uc2  close. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020121dy1l00b49\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
