\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar lifts from record low in Toronto. \b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2002\par 17:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      Reuters plans to combine coverage of the Canadian capital \par \par \uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets into one report that will have all \par \par \uc2  the usual features of both the Canadian dollar report and the \par \par \uc2  Canadian bond report. \par \par \uc2      The new report, which begins Feb. 4, will continue to be \par \par \uc2  delivered twice daily. It will be found on pages and \par \par \uc2  , the pages currently used for two separate reports. \par \par \uc2      If you have any comments, please contact Canadian Bureau \par \par \uc2  Chief Russell Blinch at russell.blinch@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2      Bank of Canada: CANADA OPEN  1.6133  PREVIOUS CLOSE 1.5993 \par \par \uc2  -------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Jan 17 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar flopped to \par \par \uc2  a record low on Thursday and the start of the North American \par \par \uc2  session saw slight relief for the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \par \par \uc2  technical selling took off with little in its way to stop the \par \par \uc2  slide. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as low as \par \par \uc2  C$1.6170 per U.S. dollar, or 61.84 U.S. cents, \par \par \uc2  plummeting through its previous record of C$1.6052, or 62.30 \par \par \uc2  U.S. cents, set on Dec. 24. \par \par \uc2  Automatic sell orders were triggered in London by the break \par \par \uc2  of key chart levels, sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down just over one \par \par \uc2  percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  "There was nothing there to defend it, to stop the flow. \par \par \uc2  All the orders that had been in the books of the major banks \par \par \uc2  between C$1.60 and C$1.6050 had been taken out one week \par \par \uc2  earlier," said Jack Spitz, regional manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  at National Bank of Canada. \par \par \uc2  "Once it pushed through the C$1.6052 (level)... there was \par \par \uc2  really nothing to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It's the abyss that \par \par \uc2  exists when the stops get taken out and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can run." \par \par \uc2  At 11:00 a.m. (1600 GMT), the Canadian dollar was at \par \par \uc2  C$1.6116 to the U.S. dollar, or 62.05 U.S. cents, down sharply \par \par \uc2  from C$1.5993, or 62.53 U.S. cents at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Spitz said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was consolidating in the Toronto \par \par \uc2  session, and he was looking for some reaction from either the \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  or Finance Minister Paul Martin. \par \par \uc2  Some talk of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  made the \par \par \uc2  rounds early in the morning, but the 9 a.m. window where the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically moves or make a statement came and went \par \par \uc2  with no sign of change. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still vulnerable to retest the new low. \par \par \uc2  "I think we are in for a continued rough period for a short \par \par \uc2  period of time as markets struggle with this idea about \par \par \uc2  adjusting expectations from a firm recovery to one that's a \par \par \uc2  little tenuous," said Mark Chandler, senior economist at \par \par \uc2  Goldman Sachs. \par \par \uc2  While some analysts shrugged off suggestions that the \par \par \uc2  Canadian dollar's new low was a direct effect of the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Canada's quarter-point rate cut earlier this week, others said \par \par \uc2  the modest cut would not be enough to revive the country's \par \par \uc2  sagging economy. \par \par \uc2  These analysts point to the Canadian dollar's rally from \par \par \uc2  roughly C$1.5950 to C$1.5850 after the overnight rate was \par \par \uc2  reduced to 2.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  In cross-trading, the Canadian dollar was at 81.95 \par \par \uc2  yen versus 82.54 yen at the previous close. Against the \par \par \uc2  Australian dollar , it was at A$1.2080, compared with \par \par \uc2  A$1.2149. Against the euro , the Canadian dollar was at \par \par \uc2  C$1.4194 versus C$1.4097 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020117dy1h00vnb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
