\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  sees only rare  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 129 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2001\par 18:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OTTAWA, Nov 29 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor David Dodge said on Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in extraordinary circumstances. \par \par \uc2  Dodge told the Senate banking committee that the Bank of Canada used to operate daily in the market to avoid major fluctuations, hour to hour or day to day. \par \par \uc2  "We stopped doing that. The market is deep and robust enough that it takes care of it itself," he said. \par \par \uc2  "So our policy, clearly enunciated, is that we don't normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets, and it would only be in extraordinary circumstances that we would consider using the tool. It is there. It can be used, but it would have to be absolutely extraordinary circumstances." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011129dxbt04gnv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
