\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2 's Dodge Says No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Help C$ \b0\par\par\uc2 179 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 01:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones News Service \par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  OTTAWA -(Dow Jones)- During a question and answer session at the Senate Committee on Banking Wednesday, Bank of Canada Governor David Dodge fended off questions about the weakening Canadian dollar and what, if anything, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could do to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  When asked if the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the dollar, Dodge said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in extraordinary circumstances or if there was a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  He said the Canadian dollar has been weakening against the U.S. dollar, along with other world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but that the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been falling against other world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would be of greater concern to him and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dodge also refuted suggestions that Canada may be heading into a recession, saying the first half of this year would be "rough" for the economy, but that there should be a positive economic rebound in the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  -Joel Baglole, Dow Jones Newswires; 613-237-0668 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020010711dx3s02y86\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgo