\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar ends flat after choppy trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2000\par 22:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      Bank of Canada: CANADA OPEN  1.5307 PREVIOUS CLOSE 1.5317 \par \par \uc2  -------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      By Don Curren \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Nov 3 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar ended down \par \par \uc2  slightly after choppy trading on Friday as the Canadian \par \par \uc2  election campaign began to cast a larger shadow over the \par \par \uc2  volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market watchers said. \par \par \uc2      The Canadian dollar closed at C$1.5327 (65.24 U.S. cents) \par \par \uc2  against C$1.5317 (65.29 U.S. cents) at the previous close. \par \par \uc2      It strengthened to the C$1.5285 area in early North \par \par \uc2  American trading after broadly supportive job news from both \par \par \uc2  Canada and the United States. It then pared some of its gains \par \par \uc2  and gravitated towards a range near Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2      "It was pretty whippy this morning," said one New \par \par \uc2  York-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a major Canadian bank. \par \par \uc2      News that employment in Canada rose 20,200 in October, \par \par \uc2  slightly exceeding the 20,000 expected by analysts, was \par \par \uc2  modestly positive for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market watchers said. \par \par \uc2      The unemployment rate rose to 6.9 percent from 6.8 percent \par \par \uc2  in September. \par \par \uc2      "I think the employment data was good. It should have \par \par \uc2  picked up a bit there, it should have picked up a bit more on \par \par \uc2  the U.S. numbers, the nonfarms being a little soft," the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. \par \par \uc2      U.S. nonfarm payrolls increased by 137,000 in October, \par \par \uc2  defying expectations of a 184,000 increase. \par \par \uc2      But the U.S. report was mixed, with some analysts pointing \par \par \uc2  to news that average hourly earnings rose 0.4 percent as \par \par \uc2  evidence that inflationary pressures are still percolating in \par \par \uc2  the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian federal election on Nov. 27, which most market \par \par \uc2  watchers say has had only a limited impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \par \par \uc2  recent volatile trading, may be starting to play a more \par \par \uc2  prominent role, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  "I think people are still looking at (the Canadian dollar), \par \par \uc2  still a little uncertain with the election coming up," he \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The fact that the incumbent Liberals are slipping a bit in \par \par \uc2  opinion polls, while the opposition Canadian Alliance party is \par \par \uc2  gaining support, may be eliciting some concern from market \par \par \uc2  players, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  A poll by Environics Research Group said the Liberals were \par \par \uc2  ahead of the right-wing Canadian Alliance party by 45 percent \par \par \uc2  to 29 percent, compared with a 44-25 spread in a poll by the \par \par \uc2  same company last week. An Ipsos-Reid poll this week put the \par \par \uc2  spread at 42 percent to 29 percent for the Liberals, compared \par \par \uc2  with 45-28 last week. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think it puts any real uncertainty into the \par \par \uc2  market, but it probably makes any international investor a \par \par \uc2  little concerned," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  EURO STRENGTH SAID DETRIMENTAL \par \par \uc2  Gains in the euro, which was boosted by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, are also \par \par \uc2  detrimental for the Canadian dollar, he added. "Obviously, the \par \par \uc2  stronger euro goes a little bit against Canada, too," the \par \par \uc2  trader said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined in on the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  on behalf of the common European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sept. 22, but \par \par \uc2  analysts believe it's unlikely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will join in \par \par \uc2  any more efforts to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short term. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to drop as low as C$1.5400, \par \par \uc2  or even C$1.5500 in coming weeks, although a Liberal victory \par \par \uc2  could help inject some new strength into the anaemic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  he added. \par \par \uc2  "I think if the Liberals get back in, we'll get some \par \par \uc2  stability back here and wouldn't be surprised to see us... down \par \par \uc2  to C$1.5100 to C$1.5200 after the election," he said. \par \par \uc2  Katherine Beattie, technical analyst at Standard & Poor's \par \par \uc2  MMS, agreed that adverse poll results for the Liberals could \par \par \uc2  hamper the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2      "If the Liberals continue to slide in the polls, that's \par \par \uc2  another negative," she said. \par \par \uc2      On the top side, the Canadian unit was unable to make it \par \par \uc2  through congestion in the C$1.5275 area during the session, she \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      "Technically, tools are a little mixed, but there's no \par \par \uc2  denying that the trend is towards a higher (U.S. dollar spot \par \par \uc2  rate), so we're going to watch C$1.5392, this week's high," \par \par \uc2  Beattie said. \par \par \uc2      A break through that area could see the U.S. dollar climb \par \par \uc2  to C$1.5488 to C$1.5500, she added. \par \par \uc2      In cross-trading against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar was at 69.78 yen, compared with 70.57 yen at the \par \par \uc2  previous session's close, and at C$1.3270 against the euro \par \par \uc2   versus C$1.3155. The Canadian dollar was at A$1.2390 \par \par \uc2   against the Australian dollar versus A$1.2534. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb302mc7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
