\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar down slightly as players focus on euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2000\par 22:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  CANADA OPEN  1.4980    PREVIOUS CLOSE  1.4940\par \tab \tab  DAILY  HIGH  1.4991    OVERNIGHT HIGH  1.4984\par \tab \tab \tab    LOW  1.4949\tab \tab    LOW  1.4949\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      By Don Curren \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Oct 5 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar ended \par \par \uc2  moderately lower on Thursday as market players focused on the \par \par \uc2  euro and the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  on behalf of the floundering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar closed at C$1.4970 (66.80 U.S. cents) \par \par \uc2  on Thursday against C$1.4940 (66.93 U.S. cents) at the previous \par \par \uc2  session's close. \par \par \uc2  "We're getting some surprises on the euro," said Steve \par \par \uc2  Demers, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at National Bank of Canada \par \par \uc2  in Montreal. \par \par \uc2  Market players remained focused on the travails of the \par \par \uc2  common European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) \par \par \uc2  raised interest rates by 25 basis points on Thursday. The \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  subsequently slumped to levels as low as 86.60 cents, \par \par \uc2  its lowest levels since central banks launched joint \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September \par \par \uc2  22. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined forces with other G7 central \par \par \uc2  banks in that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prompting concerns in earlier \par \par \uc2  sessions it might do so again, and putting some pressure on the \par \par \uc2  Canadian unit as a result, market watchers said. \par \par \uc2  Market players are becoming increasingly convinced other G7 \par \par \uc2  central banks may not join subsequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support \par \par \uc2  of the euro, Demers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is looking at a situation where if there are \par \par \uc2  more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the euro, the (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2  will go alone," Demers said. "I think more and more folks are \par \par \uc2  comfortable with the idea of the ECB going it alone if they are \par \par \uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  a second time." \par \par \uc2      That shift in perception helped keep losses in the Canadian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contained on Thursday, he added. \par \par \uc2      "That's why Canada's holding in quite well, because if we \par \par \uc2  have another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling its own \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels, I don't think the market would like \par \par \uc2  that all that much," he said. \par \par \uc2  Some of the pressure may stem from wariness ahead of U.S. \par \par \uc2  and Canadian job data scheduled for release on Friday morning, \par \par \uc2  market watchers said. \par \par \uc2      "I think we're just keeping a little bit of risk in this \par \par \uc2  thing because of tomorrow morning's numbers," Demers said. \par \par \uc2      Canadian and U.S. employment data for September, due on \par \par \uc2  Friday, are the most significant economic releases for the \par \par \uc2  week. Analysts surveyed by Reuters are calling for employment \par \par \uc2  to have increased by 28,225 in September after increasing \par \par \uc2  44,000 in August. The unemployment rate is seen dipping to 7.0 \par \par \uc2  percent in September from 7.1 percent the previous month. \par \par \uc2  "If you get good employment numbers in Canada, it feels \par \par \uc2  like (the U.S. dollar) will trade down to something like \par \par \uc2  C$1.4890 before the weekend," Demers said. \par \par \uc2      "That's with one assumption, that the Bank of Canada does \par \par \uc2  not come in if the ECB does something," he added. \par \par \uc2      In cross-trading against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar was at 72.87 yen, compared with 72.16 at the \par \par \uc2  previous session's close, and at C$1.2997 against the euro \par \par \uc2   versus C$1.3062. The Canadian dollar was at A$1.2474 \par \par \uc2   against the Australian dollar versus A$1.2434. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa505664\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
