\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar opens stronger, market sentiment turns. \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2000\par 16:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  CANADA OPEN  1.4983    PREVIOUS CLOSE  1.5042\par \tab \tab  DAILY  HIGH  1.5054    OVERNIGHT HIGH  1.5054\par \tab \tab \tab    LOW  1.5072\tab \tab    LOW  1.4967\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Oct 4 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar opened \par \par \uc2  higher on Wednesday, a reversal of market sentiment that has \par \par \uc2  seen market players taking profits and trading on merger and \par \par \uc2  acquisition flows. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was at C$1.495 (66.69 U.S. cents) on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday against C$1.5042 (66.48 U.S. cents) from the previous \par \par \uc2  session's close. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar moved from the C$1.5025 area to \par \par \uc2  strengthen to C$1.4960 in overnight trade based on two things \par \par \uc2  in particular, said Mark Abbott, vice president and senior \par \par \uc2  dealer at Societe Generale in Montreal. \par \par \uc2      Abbott said the recent sell-off in the Canadian dollar has \par \par \uc2  seen some profit-taking and consolidation in the works. \par \par \uc2      Mining and metals group Billiton Plc said on Wednesday that \par \par \uc2  it was proceeding with its C$1.7 billion offer for Canadian \par \par \uc2  mining company Rio Algom Ltd, one day after rival bidder \par \par \uc2  Noranda declined to make a counter offer. \par \par \uc2  "Whether or not that's actually going through, hey it's \par \par \uc2  just speculation... but you combine that with the mood in the \par \par \uc2  last couple of days, it's enough of a reason to make people \par \par \uc2  think the Canadian dollar is strengthening because Billiton is \par \par \uc2  going to buy all these Canadian dollars to buy Rio Algom," said \par \par \uc2  Abbott. \par \par \uc2  But, while Abbott does not subscribe to such speculation, \par \par \uc2  believing it too early, he admits that the Billiton deal is a \par \par \uc2  good "excuse" to trade. \par \par \uc2  The foreign reserves data released earlier this morning \par \par \uc2  confirmed the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  played a "minor role" in the \par \par \uc2  coordinated global \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the euro. The \par \par \uc2  Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's participation was limited to C$97 \par \par \uc2  million, versus $1.3 billion from the U.S. Federal Reserve, \par \par \uc2  according to Standard & Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  Canadian and U.S. employment data for September, due on \par \par \uc2  Friday, remain the heavyweight reports the market is waiting \par \par \uc2  for directional clues. \par \par \uc2  In cross-trading against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar was at 72.76 yen compared to 72.37 at the \par \par \uc2  previous session's close, and at C$1.3123 against the euro \par \par \uc2   versus C$1.3148. The Canadian dollar was at A$1.2414 \par \par \uc2   against the Australian dollar versus A$1.2306. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa405fxw\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (canada near10 interven*) and 